WEBVTT

00:06.206 --> 00:07.685
Previously on  From…

00:07.766 --> 00:09.205
This place is fucking with your head

00:09.286 --> 00:11.045
because it knows
how much you miss your dad.

00:11.566 --> 00:13.765
I watched you have two seizures
in two days.

00:13.846 --> 00:16.485
You're only angry at me right now
because you know I'm right.

00:18.006 --> 00:20.805
When I found Mom out by The Bottle Tree,
I saw him.

00:21.326 --> 00:22.605
He was eating her.

00:28.206 --> 00:30.285
What's wrong with you?

00:30.366 --> 00:32.845
-Show him what he did!
-Okay, okay, okay.

00:33.446 --> 00:34.965
There's something about those dolls.

00:35.526 --> 00:36.725
I think I've seen them before.

00:44.566 --> 00:45.885
-We have to--
-Donna!

00:45.966 --> 00:47.205
-Donna!
-Donna!

00:53.366 --> 00:54.565
What just happened?

00:54.646 --> 00:55.765
I remembered.

00:56.526 --> 00:58.485
I remembered how to hurt them.

00:58.566 --> 01:01.405
Boyd, I think the mushrooms kicked in.

01:03.966 --> 01:06.045
Show me what I used to know.

01:06.646 --> 01:08.765
It's me when I was 12 years old.

01:08.846 --> 01:11.965
You have to clear the way to see the path.

01:16.966 --> 01:18.885
This is where
the children were sacrificed.

01:18.966 --> 01:21.285
Tell me how we save them
when we've already failed.

01:22.726 --> 01:23.845
Hi, Jade.

01:23.926 --> 01:25.165
No! No!

01:26.566 --> 01:27.565
Anghkooey.

01:28.846 --> 01:31.765
-Jade! Jade! Hey, hey!
-How the fuck did we get here?

01:31.846 --> 01:33.685
Jade, you never left.

01:33.766 --> 01:35.445
I know what we have to do to go home.

01:36.486 --> 01:38.565
I know how we can save the children.

01:40.486 --> 01:41.805
You can't be serious.

01:41.886 --> 01:43.765
I'm telling you, it is the only way.

01:43.846 --> 01:45.645
To what? To get everyone killed?

01:45.766 --> 01:48.285
You want to go down in those tunnels
where those things live

01:48.366 --> 01:50.965
because you think the bones
of those children are buried down there?

01:51.046 --> 01:52.045
Yes!

01:53.486 --> 01:55.365
It's getting late. All right?

01:55.446 --> 01:56.605
We should get some sleep.

01:56.686 --> 02:00.485
Listen, I understand
that this all seems a little shaky.

02:00.566 --> 02:01.805
"A little shaky"?

02:01.886 --> 02:03.725
Is that how you'd describe this?
"A little shaky"?

02:03.806 --> 02:05.765
We knew going into this
it was an out-of-the-box swing.

02:05.846 --> 02:08.005
If you're just going to flatly reject
everything I found

02:08.086 --> 02:10.885
based on how I found it,
then what the fuck did I even do this for?

02:10.966 --> 02:11.965
All right, all right.

02:14.486 --> 02:15.685
All right.

02:15.766 --> 02:18.285
Let's just forget for a second
that you saw all this

02:18.366 --> 02:21.125
during a mushroom-infused fever dream.

02:21.206 --> 02:22.245
Let's just…

02:23.806 --> 02:25.925
Let's just put that aside for a second.

02:27.886 --> 02:31.285
Even if you're right, right,
and the bones are down there…

02:33.486 --> 02:34.485
so what?

02:35.606 --> 02:38.045
How does finding bones help us go home?

02:39.286 --> 02:41.005
I'm not entirely sure yet.

02:43.006 --> 02:44.005
Right.

02:51.126 --> 02:52.165
Bones.

02:52.926 --> 02:54.525
Okay, listen to me.

02:54.606 --> 02:56.845
There are countless examples
throughout history

02:57.606 --> 03:00.845
of cultures, of religions
that hold the remains…

03:01.766 --> 03:05.925
the remains of the deceased
in great reverence.

03:07.766 --> 03:10.525
What do you think the Egyptians
mummified their rulers for?

03:10.606 --> 03:14.805
This place, this fucking nightmare
that we are stuck in was built…

03:17.326 --> 03:18.525
on a sacrifice.

03:22.126 --> 03:26.365
What if the bones are what anchor
the spirits of those children here?

03:27.006 --> 03:28.605
I mean, have you ever wondered
why those creatures

03:28.686 --> 03:30.125
never come out of the tunnels
during the day?

03:30.206 --> 03:32.485
What if they're down there
protecting the very thing

03:32.566 --> 03:34.125
that makes this place possible?

03:34.646 --> 03:37.485
Which brings me back to the part
where you get everyone killed.

03:38.166 --> 03:39.645
Not if we do it right.

03:40.206 --> 03:41.205
Okay.

03:42.246 --> 03:45.085
Tell me what the right version
of this plan looks like. Just…

03:48.926 --> 03:51.245
Well, I mean,
that's sort of where you come in.

03:53.926 --> 03:56.365
Look, I realize there are
a lot of things in your head right now

03:56.446 --> 03:59.045
that may turn out to be really important,

03:59.126 --> 04:01.645
but look at it from where I'm standing.

04:02.726 --> 04:06.325
You want me to help plan a suicide mission

04:06.406 --> 04:09.605
because of some things
that you saw in a mushroom trip.

04:10.166 --> 04:12.085
What do I have to do? What do I have to do

04:12.166 --> 04:14.285
to prove to you this is real?

04:14.366 --> 04:15.405
Yeah, I don't know.

04:17.566 --> 04:18.605
The door.

04:19.246 --> 04:20.205
What?

04:20.286 --> 04:23.045
You and I went into the basement
in Colony House.

04:23.126 --> 04:24.685
I already told you, we didn't go anywhere.

04:24.766 --> 04:26.085
Yeah, that's right. We didn't.

04:27.286 --> 04:29.125
And I've never been inside
the basement of Colony House,

04:29.206 --> 04:32.005
so I would have no way of knowing
what it looks like down there.

04:32.086 --> 04:34.325
Jade, describing
the basement of Colony House

04:34.406 --> 04:36.685
-isn't going to prove--
-There was a hidden door.

04:38.726 --> 04:41.485
Do you remember seeing any doors
in the basement of Colony House?

04:43.366 --> 04:44.325
No.

04:45.686 --> 04:49.445
So if we go there, and we find that door…

04:52.246 --> 04:55.405
would you at least consider what
I'm telling you about these bones is true?

05:00.286 --> 05:01.485
It'd be a start.

05:04.446 --> 05:07.045
Come on. Here we go. All right.

05:07.806 --> 05:10.125
Explain to me why this was fun
for your generation.

05:10.206 --> 05:12.365
-We didn't have phones.
-Interesting.

05:12.446 --> 05:14.285
It's like social media from the Stone Age.

05:14.366 --> 05:16.925
This is it. This.
This is the basement I saw.

05:17.646 --> 05:18.965
It's a little more organized.

05:19.566 --> 05:22.645
Yeah, we're trying to build a narrative
for the people that came before us.

05:22.726 --> 05:24.925
-See if we missed anything.
-Boyd's just trying to keep me busy

05:25.006 --> 05:27.085
because he knows
that I want to kill myself.

05:27.566 --> 05:28.645
How's that going?

05:28.726 --> 05:30.005
I haven't slit my wrists yet.

05:30.086 --> 05:31.605
So it's going well then.

05:31.686 --> 05:32.885
What do you need?

05:32.966 --> 05:34.645
I'm looking for a secret door that I saw

05:34.726 --> 05:36.925
while I was on mushrooms
I found in the forest.

05:38.366 --> 05:39.925
People have strange conversations here.

05:44.206 --> 05:45.285
Yahtzee!

05:53.206 --> 05:54.605
Come on! Give me a hand!

05:54.686 --> 05:55.685
Okay.

05:58.846 --> 06:00.365
Just give me a hand. Come on.

06:10.366 --> 06:13.605
No, no, no.
No, no, no. It's supposed to be here.

06:13.686 --> 06:14.725
-Jade.
-It's supposed to be here.

06:14.806 --> 06:17.045
Everything else--
Everything else is exactly the same.

06:17.126 --> 06:18.125
All right.

06:18.886 --> 06:19.885
Jade.

06:21.126 --> 06:22.445
It's supposed to be here.

08:26.686 --> 08:28.245
Maybe the door-- Maybe…

08:28.766 --> 08:30.365
Maybe it's just a metaphor.

08:31.486 --> 08:33.125
Maybe the bones are a metaphor.

08:33.966 --> 08:35.485
No! No! Listen.

08:36.646 --> 08:37.565
Look.

08:37.646 --> 08:39.805
I understand that you have doubts.

08:39.886 --> 08:42.325
Okay, if the situation were reversed,
I'd have doubts too.

08:42.406 --> 08:44.445
And I realize what I'm suggesting
is incredibly risky.

08:44.526 --> 08:46.125
It's fucking suicide.

08:46.206 --> 08:47.845
Maybe-- Maybe for some, yeah.

08:48.646 --> 08:50.005
You're okay with that?

08:50.086 --> 08:53.165
What, we lose a couple of people?
Maybe a dozen?

08:53.246 --> 08:54.445
How many's too many, Jade?

08:54.526 --> 08:55.645
How many people are gonna die

08:55.726 --> 08:57.645
if you keep sitting on your goddamn hands
doing nothing?

08:57.726 --> 08:59.365
How many have you already lost, huh?

08:59.446 --> 09:01.325
What the fuck did you say to me?

09:01.406 --> 09:02.565
Say it again.

09:03.246 --> 09:04.925
-Go ahead, say it again.
-Boyd…

09:06.086 --> 09:08.725
there's only so long
that you can hold this place together

09:08.806 --> 09:10.685
with grit and good intentions.

09:12.126 --> 09:14.685
At some point, something's gonna give,
something's gonna change.

09:15.406 --> 09:16.805
You're gonna lose this whole fucking town.

09:26.046 --> 09:28.605
Don't push me, Jade.

09:29.446 --> 09:31.245
This is our chance, Boyd.

09:32.366 --> 09:35.485
I went looking for answers,
and I found answers.

09:36.086 --> 09:37.405
This is our shot.

09:46.086 --> 09:47.925
-What was that about?
-What?

09:49.806 --> 09:50.965
Let's go outside.

09:59.126 --> 10:02.645
So, Jade thinks that
digging up these bones is gonna…

10:03.246 --> 10:05.445
somehow help us get home.

10:06.006 --> 10:09.165
If the bones are even down there
in the first place, yeah.

10:09.686 --> 10:10.845
That's his theory.

10:12.166 --> 10:14.805
And Jade and Tabitha
have these memories because…

10:15.966 --> 10:17.325
-reincarnation.
-Yeah.

10:19.686 --> 10:21.125
Boyd, what do you think?

10:22.966 --> 10:27.325
If you'd asked me
before I got worms under my skin

10:27.406 --> 10:29.925
or before I found magic rocks
in the forest

10:30.006 --> 10:32.085
that protect us from monsters, what the…

10:33.926 --> 10:36.845
Look, I wasn't… I wasn't trying
to keep any of this from you.

10:37.526 --> 10:38.725
-I just…
-I know, I know, I know.

10:38.806 --> 10:41.845
And I mean things
haven't exactly been quiet lately.

10:42.566 --> 10:43.605
They have not.

10:45.806 --> 10:47.485
Remember the good old days

10:47.566 --> 10:51.045
when we used to count the nights
where nothing bad would happen?

10:51.126 --> 10:53.245
If you'd have told me
that was the good part…

10:55.406 --> 10:57.765
There is something else
we need to talk about.

10:57.846 --> 10:58.845
Look.

11:05.006 --> 11:06.605
Oh, my God. What's he doing?

11:08.406 --> 11:10.205
Hey, what's going on?

11:10.286 --> 11:11.325
Victor's on the roof.

11:11.406 --> 11:12.325
What?

11:15.486 --> 11:16.965
-Shit.
-What the…

11:18.726 --> 11:19.725
Goddammit.

11:22.246 --> 11:23.805
I don't know. He might need some help.

11:23.886 --> 11:25.365
-Is he listening?
-Victor!

11:36.966 --> 11:38.165
Pretty nice view.

11:41.046 --> 11:42.445
What are you doing up here?

11:48.246 --> 11:51.485
When I was a boy,
a man jumped from here.

11:52.966 --> 11:54.805
He hated this place so much.

11:56.246 --> 11:59.045
And he was so scared all the time,
so one day he jumped.

12:01.606 --> 12:03.805
It took days for him to finally die.

12:08.166 --> 12:10.045
He was trying to fix things…

12:11.726 --> 12:13.485
but he just made them worse.

12:19.166 --> 12:22.045
Are you here
because of what I told my dad?

12:23.726 --> 12:24.685
Yeah.

12:28.926 --> 12:30.885
I shouldn't have told him any of that.

12:32.446 --> 12:33.445
Hey, Victor.

12:35.086 --> 12:36.045
The man in the suit…

12:37.166 --> 12:39.245
he came here just like everybody else.

12:43.006 --> 12:44.965
Is there anything else
you can remember about him?

12:47.406 --> 12:49.325
Hey, hey, Victor.

12:56.926 --> 12:58.005
I can try.

12:59.606 --> 13:00.605
Okay.

13:02.486 --> 13:04.005
Why don't we go inside?

13:30.326 --> 13:31.285
Sara.

13:32.646 --> 13:34.325
-Julie.
-Hi.

13:36.806 --> 13:38.125
What's the paint for?

13:38.206 --> 13:43.165
I wanted to do something nice for Sophia,
make her feel more at home.

13:44.006 --> 13:46.885
Nathan always used to say a fresh coat
of paint will fix all your woes.

13:46.966 --> 13:50.325
I… I don't know what color's in the cans.

13:51.966 --> 13:56.005
Look, I just wanted to say I'm sorry.

13:57.286 --> 14:00.245
I didn't really understand
what you went through.

14:01.486 --> 14:03.045
But I think I do now.

14:04.166 --> 14:05.485
Yeah.

14:05.566 --> 14:06.925
Just wanted to say sorry.

14:07.806 --> 14:09.205
Do you want to help?

14:11.406 --> 14:13.325
I have an extra brush.

14:13.406 --> 14:14.525
Come on inside.

14:25.886 --> 14:27.125
This man in yellow…

14:28.646 --> 14:31.445
you told your dad he came to town
just like everybody else.

14:32.806 --> 14:34.365
I thought his suit was funny.

14:35.366 --> 14:37.245
He seemed like a nice man.

14:38.406 --> 14:40.645
-Was he alone when he came here?
-Yes.

14:41.726 --> 14:43.365
I think so. I don't know. I'm not sure.

14:43.966 --> 14:46.165
Do you remember
what kind of car he came in?

14:47.806 --> 14:49.205
It was big and it was…

14:49.846 --> 14:51.325
it was brown.

14:53.446 --> 14:56.365
Big and brown. Is that one of the cars
you took out to the woods?

14:56.446 --> 14:58.005
I didn't want to see it.

14:58.086 --> 14:59.405
Okay.

15:00.646 --> 15:03.285
Hey, you think
you could go out there with us

15:03.366 --> 15:05.125
and show us which one it is?

15:09.206 --> 15:10.725
Victor. Hey, hey, Victor.

15:11.246 --> 15:14.125
I'm not going to make you do anything
that you don't want to do, okay?

15:14.206 --> 15:17.605
We just need to get
as much information as we can.

15:18.726 --> 15:22.165
We need to find out if this guy,
this man, whatever he is,

15:22.246 --> 15:24.285
if it's something
that we've gotta worry about.

15:25.406 --> 15:27.005
Just trying to keep everybody safe.

15:28.126 --> 15:29.325
Will you help me do that?

15:30.326 --> 15:32.045
-Hey, it's-- Okay.
-Okay.

15:32.686 --> 15:34.525
Boyd? You in there?

15:35.206 --> 15:36.205
What…

15:38.526 --> 15:40.605
Hey, what are you doing back so soon?

15:41.326 --> 15:43.285
You need to come down to the shed.

15:45.606 --> 15:46.765
Come on.

15:52.526 --> 15:53.885
Hey, you doing okay?

15:53.966 --> 15:56.285
-Have you seen Victor?
-Yeah. He's up in his room.

16:00.766 --> 16:01.725
Where's Ellis?

16:01.806 --> 16:04.205
He's fine.
He went inside to check on Fatima.

16:04.726 --> 16:07.205
Patty's down at the clinic.
She got pretty banged up.

16:07.286 --> 16:08.325
How?

16:09.966 --> 16:11.485
Let's go inside.

16:21.566 --> 16:23.325
The fuck, Donna? Who is that?

16:24.286 --> 16:25.765
It was Roger.

16:28.446 --> 16:31.125
I don't know how else to say this,
so I'm just gonna say it.

16:33.446 --> 16:36.205
We were attacked by giant dolls…

16:37.006 --> 16:38.805
that came out of the lake.

16:40.646 --> 16:41.805
And these?

16:42.806 --> 16:44.205
Not just decorative.

16:45.246 --> 16:48.925
Tabitha used it to kill one of the dolls.

16:49.686 --> 16:52.965
Drove it right through the fucker.
The rest just walked away.

16:55.286 --> 16:56.405
Sadly…

16:58.206 --> 17:01.485
that was after they got ahold of Roger.

17:04.886 --> 17:06.565
We found his body this morning.

17:10.086 --> 17:11.405
Jesus.

17:14.366 --> 17:16.765
We left some food
back up at the settlement

17:16.846 --> 17:18.765
so we could bring back the totems.

17:19.806 --> 17:23.445
We figured they'd be worth more
than a few bags of turnips.

17:27.446 --> 17:30.925
Anybody need a drink?
Because I need a drink.

17:35.766 --> 17:38.365
-Say something.
-It's just a lot to take in.

17:40.486 --> 17:41.605
I'm not crazy.

17:41.686 --> 17:42.685
No, I…

17:43.206 --> 17:45.645
No, I know. I know. That's not…

17:46.966 --> 17:49.325
After everything that
this place has done to you,

17:49.406 --> 17:52.165
with everything that
this place is still doing to you,

17:52.246 --> 17:54.525
I just don't understand what's happening.

17:55.286 --> 17:56.405
Okay? And I just--

17:56.486 --> 18:00.485
I feel like there is just so much more
that I should be doing to help.

18:00.566 --> 18:03.485
And I feel like
I am the one that's failing here.

18:03.566 --> 18:05.845
-No, babe--
-No, I know. And I'm not just--

18:05.926 --> 18:08.205
I'm not just saying that so that you'll…

18:10.766 --> 18:11.805
Look, just…

18:15.366 --> 18:16.845
Just help me understand.

18:22.366 --> 18:25.605
Growing up, there were
a lot of times when I was afraid.

18:26.726 --> 18:29.165
A lot of times when I felt powerless.

18:29.246 --> 18:32.925
But those stories about the Jinn,

18:33.006 --> 18:36.365
Vishnu and Krishna,
the Golem of Prague…

18:38.846 --> 18:41.805
I understand now
why my father told me those stories.

18:43.246 --> 18:45.685
The world was so fucking scary.

18:46.326 --> 18:49.325
But if I could believe
in magical things, then…

18:51.286 --> 18:53.245
that was something
no one could ever take away.

18:54.846 --> 18:57.605
Look, we have seen so much darkness.

18:58.286 --> 19:00.565
We live with so much fear.

19:01.206 --> 19:03.845
I need to believe in magical things.

19:10.526 --> 19:11.525
Victor?

19:13.966 --> 19:14.965
Hi.

19:15.966 --> 19:17.165
What are you doing?

19:17.886 --> 19:22.125
I'm trying to remember stuff. Bad stuff.

19:24.006 --> 19:26.485
Is this about the suit
we found in the forest?

19:30.006 --> 19:31.645
Why did you get so scared?

19:33.806 --> 19:35.485
I don't want to tell you that.

19:35.566 --> 19:36.925
Why not?

19:37.006 --> 19:41.205
Because I told my dad, he got…
he got really upset.

19:41.286 --> 19:42.485
Why?

19:42.566 --> 19:45.525
I just told you
I don't want to tell you that.

19:48.886 --> 19:51.005
Well, then,
I guess I'm not going to tell you

19:51.086 --> 19:52.645
what happened at the settlement.

19:55.446 --> 19:56.405
Fine.

19:59.806 --> 20:01.005
Can I draw with you?

20:06.486 --> 20:07.485
Yes.

20:33.406 --> 20:35.085
The lake had monsters in it.

20:37.366 --> 20:38.965
What kind of monsters?

20:39.046 --> 20:40.405
Giant dolls.

20:42.566 --> 20:43.525
Really?

20:48.966 --> 20:50.725
What did your mom do?

20:50.806 --> 20:52.485
My mom killed one.

20:54.846 --> 20:57.725
Your mom's pretty tough.

21:00.486 --> 21:01.525
Yeah.

21:01.606 --> 21:05.125
Well, my mom was pretty tough, too.

21:06.126 --> 21:07.365
You know, she was always…

21:07.446 --> 21:10.165
She always smiled even if she was scared.

21:11.246 --> 21:14.245
Because she knew that
we would be scared if she didn't.

21:17.926 --> 21:20.045
I don't think my dad's that strong.

21:42.526 --> 21:45.245
Excuse me. Have you seen the sheriff?

21:45.926 --> 21:47.365
No. He…

21:48.086 --> 21:50.525
Try up at Colony House, maybe.

21:50.606 --> 21:51.645
Thanks.

21:55.686 --> 21:57.005
Your name is Henry, right?

21:57.646 --> 21:58.725
That's right.

21:59.926 --> 22:01.645
You look troubled, Henry.

22:02.846 --> 22:06.125
Well, it's been a bit of a day.

22:07.006 --> 22:08.125
Excuse me.

22:25.286 --> 22:26.485
You again, huh?

22:29.006 --> 22:32.365
Why is there a bar
inside of a gas station?

22:33.286 --> 22:35.765
Better question is,
why is there a gas station

22:35.846 --> 22:37.725
in a town where no one can leave?

22:38.366 --> 22:39.765
That's a good point.

22:43.206 --> 22:44.645
Who makes the alcohol?

22:45.766 --> 22:50.005
It's my understanding
there used to be a bartender here.

22:50.846 --> 22:52.565
He's dead now, of course.

22:54.726 --> 22:56.325
Do you mind if I join you?

23:00.686 --> 23:03.285
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to bother you.

23:03.366 --> 23:07.005
No, sit, please. I didn't mean to be rude.

23:11.606 --> 23:13.565
I get it. Trust me.

23:13.646 --> 23:16.685
It's kind of amazing that anyone here

23:16.766 --> 23:19.125
has the capacity
to do anything even remotely…

23:19.206 --> 23:22.805
Here's to the resiliency
of the human spirit.

23:24.006 --> 23:25.725
Let's be resilient together.

23:26.286 --> 23:27.285
I'd like that.

23:29.006 --> 23:30.365
How old are you?

23:31.566 --> 23:33.485
Old enough to have buried my dad.

23:34.326 --> 23:35.725
Old enough to grieve.

23:36.646 --> 23:37.685
Touché.

23:46.966 --> 23:47.965
All right.

23:48.566 --> 23:52.965
So you're saying that those things
that attacked you, right, you're say--

23:53.046 --> 23:55.445
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. What are you saying?

23:56.606 --> 23:59.405
They were my dolls. I was a little girl.

23:59.486 --> 24:01.485
The man who took them from me
was afraid of them.

24:01.566 --> 24:03.765
He said they gave him nightmares.

24:04.286 --> 24:05.405
So he threw them in the lake.

24:05.846 --> 24:07.405
But then when the man died…

24:08.966 --> 24:10.285
somehow they came to life.

24:11.606 --> 24:13.325
Our fears become part of the forest.

24:14.646 --> 24:15.765
What?

24:16.486 --> 24:18.645
When the cicadas were all over town,

24:18.726 --> 24:21.405
Sara told me Nathan
had always been terrified of them.

24:22.566 --> 24:26.125
She thought that maybe the people
who die here, that their fears,

24:26.206 --> 24:28.845
their nightmares
become part of the forest.

24:33.126 --> 24:35.485
-I think she was right.
-Goddammit.

24:37.446 --> 24:39.805
-Donna--
-How are we gonna tell people?

24:40.606 --> 24:43.645
How are we gonna tell them
that they not only have to worry

24:43.726 --> 24:46.685
about those smiling pieces of shit
that come out at night,

24:46.766 --> 24:51.005
but now we have literal fucking nightmares

24:51.086 --> 24:52.885
that we can't even protect them from?

24:52.966 --> 24:55.405
How much more can people take
before we just--

24:55.486 --> 24:57.565
-Why don't you just have a seat?
-No, look.

24:57.646 --> 25:00.605
I just need to splash some water
on my face.

25:02.446 --> 25:03.965
-Hey, Donna! Donna!
-Donna?

25:04.526 --> 25:06.965
Hey, Donna, Donna. Donna, Donna.

25:07.046 --> 25:08.365
Hey, Donna.

25:08.446 --> 25:10.645
-Hey, Donna.
-Donna!

25:10.726 --> 25:12.965
Donna, talk to me. Donna, talk to me.

25:14.566 --> 25:16.165
-Go get Kristi now.
-Yeah.

25:16.246 --> 25:17.565
-Take the van.
-Yeah!

25:17.646 --> 25:19.645
Donna. Hey, do you know
how to check for a pulse?

25:19.726 --> 25:21.205
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

25:24.166 --> 25:26.125
Come on, Donna. Come on.

25:27.966 --> 25:29.685
-I found the ointment.
-Oh, great.

25:29.766 --> 25:31.445
-There's not much left.
-Okay.

25:33.566 --> 25:34.525
Okay.

25:35.326 --> 25:36.605
This is gonna sting, okay?

25:36.686 --> 25:39.445
But it's gonna keep it
nice and clean, okay?

25:43.126 --> 25:47.245
Just breathe.
I know. You're doing great. Good.

25:48.446 --> 25:50.925
You're okay, just breathe.
I know. Just breathe.

25:51.006 --> 25:52.285
Press this here.

25:53.846 --> 25:54.765
There we go.

25:54.846 --> 25:56.085
Kristi!

25:56.726 --> 25:59.045
-Donna had a heart attack.
-What?

25:59.126 --> 26:01.325
Come on, Donna. Stay with me.

26:03.086 --> 26:05.285
Hey, watch out.
Clear the way. Back it up.

26:05.366 --> 26:07.165
-Does she have a pulse?
-What?

26:07.246 --> 26:08.845
No, no, no. She doesn't. She doesn't.

26:08.926 --> 26:10.965
-How long has it been?
-I don't know. Five, seven minutes.

26:11.046 --> 26:12.285
I don't know.

26:12.366 --> 26:14.245
Okay. You started compressions right away?

26:14.326 --> 26:15.845
-Here.
-Okay.

26:16.646 --> 26:17.925
-Clear.
-Yeah.

26:22.646 --> 26:24.445
-Okay. Continue compressions.
-Okay.

26:27.766 --> 26:29.205
Come on, Donna. Come on!

26:29.286 --> 26:30.805
Okay, pulse check.

26:33.086 --> 26:34.525
-No pulse.
-Okay.

26:39.166 --> 26:40.845
Okay. Continue compressions.

26:41.646 --> 26:42.965
Okay, come on, Donna.

26:44.766 --> 26:46.685
Okay, pulse check.

26:49.246 --> 26:50.205
No.

26:50.926 --> 26:51.925
Clear.

26:55.246 --> 26:56.485
Okay, go.

26:58.446 --> 26:59.685
Come on, Donna.

27:01.846 --> 27:03.005
Okay, pulse check.

27:03.086 --> 27:04.125
Come on.

27:06.406 --> 27:07.445
No.

27:08.806 --> 27:09.765
What?

27:09.846 --> 27:11.725
-No, no, no.
-Come on. Hit her again.

27:12.926 --> 27:13.925
Hit her again.

27:18.926 --> 27:20.725
Boyd. Boyd, it's not going to work.

27:20.806 --> 27:22.565
I said hit her again!

27:22.646 --> 27:24.405
Hey! Don't you do this.

27:26.766 --> 27:29.205
You don't die until I say you die.
You hear me?

27:29.846 --> 27:33.205
You don't die until I say you die.

27:33.286 --> 27:35.525
Open your fucking eyes!

27:38.446 --> 27:39.925
-Whoa, whoa.
-What was that? Did you see that?

27:40.006 --> 27:41.005
-Yeah.
-Did you see it?

27:41.086 --> 27:42.965
Her pulse is back.
It's weak, but it's back.

27:43.046 --> 27:45.965
-Donna? Hey, Donna, can you hear me?
-Is she okay? Why isn't she…

27:46.046 --> 27:48.205
I don't know, but we need the monitor
from the ambulance.

27:48.286 --> 27:50.485
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. I got it. I got it.
-You got it? Okay.

27:50.566 --> 27:52.405
-How are we going to power them up here?
-Power it?

27:52.486 --> 27:54.245
Don't worry about that.
I'll take care of that.

27:54.326 --> 27:56.085
You just take care of her, okay?

27:56.166 --> 27:57.965
Donna, can you hear me?

27:58.046 --> 28:00.245
I haven't seen one of these in years.

28:00.326 --> 28:01.605
-Look at this.
-Jade!

28:01.686 --> 28:03.685
-Hey, where are the wires?
-The what?

28:03.766 --> 28:06.205
I'm sorry. The extra wires
for the radio tower. Where are they?

28:06.286 --> 28:07.925
-What's going on?
-Donna had a heart attack.

28:08.006 --> 28:09.125
-What?
-Jesus.

28:09.206 --> 28:11.045
-Jade, where are the fucking wires?
-It's out in the shed.

28:11.126 --> 28:12.405
Come on. Come on. Go.

28:18.366 --> 28:20.965
-What the fuck is this?
-There was a problem at the settlement.

28:21.046 --> 28:23.045
-Who? Who is this?
-Jade! The wire.

28:23.126 --> 28:24.845
It's under the thing.

28:24.966 --> 28:27.325
Okay, help me move him.
Come on. Yeah, ready?

28:27.406 --> 28:29.205
-Yeah.
-One, two, three.

28:30.326 --> 28:32.125
Sweet Jesus! Fuck!

28:32.206 --> 28:35.485
Jade, hey, I promise
I'll explain everything later.

28:37.086 --> 28:38.605
Jade! I need your help.

28:38.686 --> 28:41.365
Donna needs your help.
Get your shit together.

28:41.446 --> 28:43.085
-Okay, all right.
-Thank you.

28:43.166 --> 28:44.165
Get the wires.

28:48.526 --> 28:49.805
Look-- Watch out.

28:51.766 --> 28:54.005
What's going on in there?
Is she gonna be okay?

29:01.846 --> 29:02.845
Mom?

29:03.766 --> 29:05.925
-What happened?
-I thought you were outside.

29:08.166 --> 29:10.285
Why is everyone sitting by Donna's room?

29:14.286 --> 29:15.525
Donna had a heart attack.

29:18.286 --> 29:19.645
But she's okay, right?

29:20.406 --> 29:22.805
-Is she okay?
-We don't know yet.

29:23.886 --> 29:25.565
Everyone's doing whatever they can.

29:25.646 --> 29:26.925
Hey.

29:27.006 --> 29:28.605
But she was fine.

29:28.686 --> 29:30.765
-Is it because of the settlement?
-No.

29:30.846 --> 29:33.085
-Because of the dolls?
-No, no, no. It's…

29:34.486 --> 29:37.805
Honey, sometimes things
like this just happen to people.

29:37.886 --> 29:39.645
-I want to go see her.
-Ethan.

29:39.726 --> 29:41.325
I want to see her before she dies.

29:41.406 --> 29:44.205
Hey, don't say that. She's not gonna die.

29:44.286 --> 29:45.725
Yes, she is.

29:45.806 --> 29:48.365
Everyone here dies, so please…

29:49.566 --> 29:51.005
just let me say goodbye.

29:51.886 --> 29:52.885
Please.

30:03.366 --> 30:04.325
Okay.

30:05.126 --> 30:06.685
Almost-- Almost got it.

30:08.766 --> 30:09.925
Okay, we got it.

30:10.526 --> 30:11.565
All right, well?

30:11.646 --> 30:15.685
Well, her vitals are really stable,
which is good.

30:16.766 --> 30:19.205
Okay. Then why isn't she awake?

30:21.526 --> 30:22.925
Hey, no, talk to me.

30:24.846 --> 30:28.245
Well, we just don't know how long
her brain's been deprived of oxygen for.

30:29.806 --> 30:31.405
She's gonna wake up.

30:33.366 --> 30:34.605
Kristi?

30:35.446 --> 30:36.485
I don't know.

30:40.766 --> 30:41.765
Hey.

30:43.606 --> 30:47.445
Tabitha's asking if she could
bring Ethan in here for a second.

30:47.526 --> 30:48.885
He's just really upset.

30:49.566 --> 30:51.445
Yeah, just for a second, though.

30:51.526 --> 30:52.525
Okay.

30:58.926 --> 30:59.925
Donna?

31:03.886 --> 31:05.525
I won't forget what you said.

31:08.166 --> 31:10.085
That fear is what makes us heroes.

31:15.206 --> 31:17.605
I promise I'll always do my best
to be brave.

31:24.606 --> 31:25.685
I love you, Donna.

31:42.446 --> 31:44.085
That doesn't get any better, does it?

31:44.166 --> 31:46.445
No, it does not.

31:47.566 --> 31:52.045
And that, it seems, is the end of that.

31:56.446 --> 31:59.885
I say we go for bottle number two.

31:59.966 --> 32:03.445
My dear, I cannot find it
in my heart to disagree.

32:04.846 --> 32:06.205
I can get it.

32:30.566 --> 32:32.245
Can I ask you something?

32:32.326 --> 32:33.445
Fire away.

32:39.686 --> 32:43.365
Why were you staring at that suit
in the sheriff's station?

32:48.366 --> 32:50.925
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to pry.

32:51.006 --> 32:53.605
No, it's all right. It's just…

32:56.486 --> 32:58.325
the man who wore that suit…

33:00.286 --> 33:03.845
he did things to my family.

33:05.926 --> 33:07.405
He did horrible things.

33:08.446 --> 33:09.885
You have family here?

33:10.566 --> 33:12.925
Well, just my son now.

33:14.286 --> 33:16.525
He came here with my wife and daughter…

33:17.686 --> 33:20.405
40 years ago.

33:21.646 --> 33:25.165
And that man, where is he now?

33:25.246 --> 33:27.325
Rotting in hell, I hope.

33:32.966 --> 33:34.725
I say we drink to your family.

33:35.766 --> 33:36.965
And to your father.

33:37.766 --> 33:39.165
And to my dad.

33:44.526 --> 33:45.525
Wait.

33:46.446 --> 33:50.405
There has to be something around here
that'll make that taste better.

33:50.486 --> 33:51.325
There's not.

33:51.406 --> 33:53.645
Trust me, I've looked.

33:54.926 --> 33:58.765
Well, maybe you didn't look hard en--

34:01.926 --> 34:03.125
What happened?

34:05.566 --> 34:06.925
Just some broken glass.

34:08.486 --> 34:09.565
Well, now…

34:10.486 --> 34:12.485
that doesn't look too bad. Let me see.

34:12.566 --> 34:16.725
There's got to be a clean rag
around here somewhere.

34:25.166 --> 34:27.365
You closed? What are you doing?

34:27.446 --> 34:29.885
I'm going to make food
for everyone up at Colony House.

34:29.966 --> 34:31.125
Why?

34:31.206 --> 34:33.645
Donna. She had a heart attack.

34:35.806 --> 34:36.845
Shit.

34:38.366 --> 34:39.685
Is she okay?

34:39.766 --> 34:40.965
We don't know yet.

34:42.406 --> 34:43.765
You want some help?

34:44.846 --> 34:46.205
That'd be nice.

34:46.286 --> 34:47.445
Let me take that.

34:53.646 --> 34:55.645
It's weird doing something normal.

34:56.726 --> 34:58.645
I'd almost forgotten what it was like.

35:00.766 --> 35:02.165
What do you miss most?

35:02.726 --> 35:05.005
Like, not the obvious things,
the little things.

35:08.886 --> 35:09.845
Candy.

35:11.326 --> 35:14.445
I miss candy. I had a real sweet tooth.

35:17.686 --> 35:18.845
What?

35:18.926 --> 35:20.005
Nothing.

35:20.886 --> 35:24.325
I'm trying to picture you on a couch
somewhere eating a box of Milk Duds.

35:25.806 --> 35:29.645
I was more partial
to gummy worms, gummy bears,

35:30.246 --> 35:31.565
really all things gummy.

35:31.646 --> 35:32.885
I like donuts.

35:34.726 --> 35:35.805
Donuts.

35:37.246 --> 35:40.365
Yeah, I forgot about donuts.

35:42.646 --> 35:45.125
There's this store
that my dad used to take me to,

35:45.246 --> 35:47.405
this donut shop, when I was a little girl.

35:48.646 --> 35:50.685
Just me and him.

35:51.846 --> 35:54.605
A stupid daddy-daughter thing.

35:56.926 --> 35:58.725
But one day, I…

36:00.006 --> 36:01.845
I told him I didn't want to go anymore…

36:02.846 --> 36:04.725
'cause I wanted
to hang out with my friends.

36:07.286 --> 36:08.845
I wish that I…

36:22.846 --> 36:24.965
Can I ask you something?

36:27.046 --> 36:28.005
Sure.

36:30.086 --> 36:34.125
Before, you said
you understood what I went through.

36:36.526 --> 36:37.525
How?

36:40.726 --> 36:46.125
Something here convinced me
that I could still help my dad.

36:48.726 --> 36:51.085
Like I could go back
to the day it happened and…

36:53.086 --> 36:54.845
I could save him.

37:00.126 --> 37:01.405
I can't do that.

37:02.846 --> 37:03.885
Can I?

37:20.966 --> 37:23.485
I'm so sorry that happened to you.

37:41.726 --> 37:42.685
Hey.

37:44.366 --> 37:47.405
-Any news?
-No, nothing. Nothing yet.

37:48.126 --> 37:49.885
You… You talk to Fatima?

37:50.726 --> 37:51.725
Yeah.

37:52.246 --> 37:53.285
And?

37:55.726 --> 37:58.525
Well, my wife is building a monster
in a room full of dirt.

37:59.726 --> 38:01.125
And yet it…

38:01.206 --> 38:03.285
I think it's exactly
what she needs right now.

38:03.366 --> 38:04.365
-Yeah.
-So…

38:10.806 --> 38:12.005
She awake?

38:12.526 --> 38:13.765
No, not yet.

38:18.686 --> 38:20.525
You can go sit with her if you want.

38:30.566 --> 38:32.245
-Hey.
-Hey.

38:35.006 --> 38:36.365
I'll give you some space.

38:37.246 --> 38:38.365
All right.

38:40.846 --> 38:42.685
If anything changes, you let me know.

38:42.766 --> 38:43.765
Yeah.

38:44.446 --> 38:46.165
-I'll just be outside.
-Okay.

38:57.646 --> 39:00.325
All right, you can cut the shit now
and open your eyes.

39:08.006 --> 39:09.125
I want you…

39:11.086 --> 39:12.405
to listen to me.

39:13.566 --> 39:14.565
Okay?

39:16.646 --> 39:17.845
I cannot…

39:23.486 --> 39:24.805
I cannot do this…

39:26.126 --> 39:27.565
without you.

39:27.646 --> 39:29.845
So you better wake the hell up.

39:30.766 --> 39:32.125
You hear me?

39:32.926 --> 39:35.005
We got things to do, you and me.

39:37.446 --> 39:39.005
I'm not saying goodbye.

39:39.926 --> 39:41.005
You understand?

39:42.646 --> 39:44.645
I ain't fucking saying goodbye.

39:48.486 --> 39:50.605
What are you gonna do
if she doesn't wake up?

39:52.126 --> 39:53.645
The hell kind of question is that?

39:54.606 --> 39:56.205
Practical one.

40:00.166 --> 40:02.245
Make sure you get those nice and thin.

40:02.326 --> 40:03.645
I said I'd help,

40:03.726 --> 40:06.045
not cut off my fingers
for a pot of your stew.

40:06.126 --> 40:07.525
It's really good stew.

40:11.726 --> 40:13.245
Make them a little bit chunkier.

40:14.606 --> 40:16.005
Why are you lurking
over there in the corner?

40:16.086 --> 40:17.485
Get in here and chop some veggies.

40:18.086 --> 40:19.925
-Oh, no, I was…
-I wasn't asking.

40:21.646 --> 40:22.685
Okay.

40:35.366 --> 40:37.165
We're a handsome fucking pair, huh?

40:42.686 --> 40:47.645
You remember the night that me,
Abby, and Ellis rolled into town?

40:49.046 --> 40:50.085
Yeah.

40:50.806 --> 40:52.925
Pretty sure Abby wanted you to shoot me.

40:53.646 --> 40:55.565
You scared the shit out of us,

40:55.646 --> 40:58.685
running into the middle of the street
like a goddamn lunatic.

40:59.246 --> 41:02.445
Then you bring us down
to some dugout bunker,

41:03.526 --> 41:04.885
and there was Donna.

41:06.926 --> 41:09.525
And Dale. Dale was there too, you know?

41:10.846 --> 41:12.885
Remember the first question
Donna asked me?

41:14.806 --> 41:15.765
No.

41:16.486 --> 41:18.045
"Do any of you snore?"

41:22.086 --> 41:24.405
I didn't know
what the fuck she was talking about.

41:24.486 --> 41:28.365
We just heard monsters
screeching in the forest

41:28.446 --> 41:29.765
and then climbed into a hole.

41:29.846 --> 41:31.965
And this lady is talking about snoring.

41:33.526 --> 41:36.125
Then she looked at me
calm and steady and said…

41:37.206 --> 41:39.325
"If you snore, they'll find us."

41:41.006 --> 41:44.365
Right there in the middle
of all the fear, the disbelief,

41:44.446 --> 41:47.045
the pants-shitting chaos,

41:48.246 --> 41:51.045
a little voice in the back
of my head said, "This one…

41:53.326 --> 41:55.165
yeah, she knows how to survive."

41:57.326 --> 41:58.685
"We might be okay."

42:01.246 --> 42:02.885
That's what got me through that night.

42:04.766 --> 42:08.045
Darkest, scariest night of my life,
and she's the one that got me through it.

42:10.286 --> 42:11.925
I don't think I ever told her that.

42:13.846 --> 42:17.365
We-- Did we bump heads in the beginning.

42:17.446 --> 42:21.965
She made it very clear
that she did not like me at all.

42:22.526 --> 42:23.565
No, sir.

42:25.086 --> 42:26.445
So what changed?

42:27.686 --> 42:29.525
I don't know, I like to think that…

42:31.046 --> 42:33.165
we got to know each other a little.

42:38.166 --> 42:40.845
The answer is I don't have
the slightest fucking idea.

42:41.806 --> 42:42.925
Answer to what?

42:43.006 --> 42:45.485
You asked me what I was gonna do
if she didn't wake up.

42:46.166 --> 42:48.125
Then it's time to get these people home.

42:49.566 --> 42:51.325
Look, this might not be the moment
to bring this up,

42:51.406 --> 42:53.765
but Jade already told you
what you need to do.

42:54.686 --> 42:57.445
You really just gonna ignore that
over a missing door?

42:58.086 --> 42:59.805
I mean, the fact that
Donna's lying here right now--

42:59.886 --> 43:02.885
No, you're right.
This is not the goddamn moment.

43:07.126 --> 43:08.205
Boyd?

43:13.166 --> 43:14.485
Hey, hey, hey.

43:15.926 --> 43:16.965
It's okay.

43:17.766 --> 43:19.565
No, no, no. No, you're okay.

43:19.646 --> 43:20.925
Boyd?

43:21.006 --> 43:23.845
Hey, you're here. You're okay. Kristi!

43:23.926 --> 43:26.085
-You're here. You're here.
-What?

43:26.166 --> 43:28.045
Get in here. Get in here. Get in.

43:28.126 --> 43:30.805
You're okay. You're okay.

43:30.886 --> 43:32.125
-You're all right.
-Donna.

43:32.766 --> 43:34.685
-Hey, Donna.
-Oh, God.

43:34.766 --> 43:36.205
I know. Can you look at me?

43:36.286 --> 43:37.925
-Donna, just breathe.
-Hey.

43:38.006 --> 43:39.005
Good.

43:39.646 --> 43:40.605
Yeah.

43:44.126 --> 43:46.205
Okay, I need you
to squeeze my hands, okay?

43:48.046 --> 43:49.085
Okay.

43:52.806 --> 43:54.525
-Dad?
-Yeah.

43:55.366 --> 43:56.845
-She's awake.
-Oh, my God.

43:56.926 --> 43:57.965
She's…

43:58.766 --> 44:00.045
Hey, would you…

44:00.766 --> 44:02.365
Would you tell everybody?

44:02.446 --> 44:03.485
Thank you.

44:04.166 --> 44:05.165
Yeah.

44:06.486 --> 44:07.885
-Hey, guys, she's awake.
-Yeah.

44:07.966 --> 44:09.565
-Hey, did you hear that?
-Yeah.

44:10.166 --> 44:11.565
Guys, she's awake.

44:11.646 --> 44:12.725
Hey.

44:13.486 --> 44:16.245
-She's okay?
-Yeah. Yeah, she is.

44:16.326 --> 44:18.765
-Okay.
-She's… Yeah.

44:18.846 --> 44:20.685
-Okay.
-I'll be-- I'll…

44:23.566 --> 44:26.085
There you go. Good as new.

44:26.166 --> 44:27.325
Sort of.

44:27.406 --> 44:29.645
Should we drink to my good health?

44:29.726 --> 44:30.845
Why not?

44:39.926 --> 44:41.525
That one had some kick.

44:43.366 --> 44:45.405
You know what I was thinking, Henry?

44:45.486 --> 44:47.005
I do not,

44:47.086 --> 44:50.365
but I am near certain
you are about to tell me.

44:50.446 --> 44:53.165
It's the strangest thought,
but I just can't shake it.

44:54.246 --> 44:57.725
You know, we're trapped
in a town we can't escape from,

44:58.366 --> 45:01.925
surrounded by monsters
that come from the forest at night.

45:03.366 --> 45:05.365
None of it feels real, does it?

45:07.366 --> 45:10.685
Have you ever wondered
if maybe this is all just a dream?

45:17.806 --> 45:19.045
Here we go.

45:24.366 --> 45:26.005
Great news about Donna.

45:26.966 --> 45:30.125
It's just too bad about Roger.

45:31.566 --> 45:34.125
You can't let me have
a fucking minute, can you?

45:35.686 --> 45:36.845
I'm sorry.

45:38.086 --> 45:40.445
Take as much time as you need.
I'm sure it's fine.

45:41.886 --> 45:45.725
It's not as though murderous dolls
climbed out of a lake

45:45.806 --> 45:47.045
and attacked your people.

45:47.126 --> 45:48.165
All right.

45:49.446 --> 45:50.965
What Tabitha said.

45:51.046 --> 45:52.285
About people's fears.

45:52.366 --> 45:54.765
The nightmares becoming
part of the forest after they die.

45:54.846 --> 45:56.005
Is that true?

45:56.086 --> 45:57.565
I think it might be, yeah.

45:58.366 --> 45:59.605
"Tip of the spear."

46:00.326 --> 46:01.565
What's that?

46:02.766 --> 46:05.445
This guy named Martin once told me
that those things that come out at night,

46:05.526 --> 46:07.325
they're just the tip of the spear.

46:09.046 --> 46:10.685
The bones of those kids,
are they down there?

46:10.766 --> 46:12.325
-Are they in the tunnels?
-I don't know.

46:12.406 --> 46:14.885
-What the fuck do you know?
-That you're running out of time.

46:15.406 --> 46:18.405
Hey, how am I supposed
to take people down into those tunnels

46:18.486 --> 46:21.045
when I don't have a fucking clue
if what Jade saw is even real?

46:21.126 --> 46:23.525
Some things you just have
to take on faith.

46:24.166 --> 46:25.125
I…

46:40.366 --> 46:42.205
Not with something like this.

47:16.286 --> 47:18.645
You wanna fuck with me, huh?

47:27.766 --> 47:29.445
You wanna test me, huh?

47:34.686 --> 47:35.885
What the hell?

47:40.366 --> 47:42.045
You wanna fuck with me?

47:46.766 --> 47:49.045
You want me to go down in those tunnels?

47:51.366 --> 47:53.165
You want me to risk people's lives?

47:53.806 --> 47:56.445
Then show me the fucking door!

48:16.726 --> 48:17.925
Holy shit.

48:20.606 --> 48:22.085
We're gonna need a plan.
